==================================================================================
 (2) the descent's payoff: 2-SHEET CV bounded vs 14-SHEET CV unbounded (HYP-3554), small cores
==================================================================================
   core O (odd, |O| small) | m(lonely) | CV(N2) 2-sheet | CV(N14) 14-sheet
   [1]                      | 0.8571    |        0.264  |        0.000
   [1, 3]                   | 0.7619    |        0.328  |        0.044
   [1, 3, 5]                | 0.6476    |        0.383  |        0.094
   [1, 2, 3]                | 0.6905    |        0.523  |        0.049
   [1, 3, 5, 9]             | 0.5524    |        0.534  |        0.120
   [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]          | 0.5048    |        0.683  |        0.253
   => for SMALL cores the 2-sheet CV is modest; the descent peels to small cores where CV is tame,
      converting the unbounded 14-sheet variance route (HYP-3554) into bounded 2-sheet pieces --
      EXCEPT the top large core, where both blow up (the localized gap).

==================================================================================
 (4) the least-eigenvalue certificate g is BOUNDED in [4cos^2(3pi/7), 2] (never blows up):
==================================================================================
   g range over proper cores = [0.1981, 2.0]  (m-INDEPENDENT, discrete)
   so where the measure CS bound dies (top, m'->0), the least-eigenvalue certificate persists --
   it is exactly the robust object for the open top levels (the cusp regime).
